// Storage shelf resupply on its own, for working out why the context menu stays open.
// Needs: stand within reach of the shelf. It asks for the shelf once and keeps it in the profile.
//
// The shelf context menu has two entries, Restock at 0 and Resupply at 1, so the numbers are
// not in doubt. What is in doubt is whether the entry is being selected at all: the menu opens
// and stays open, which is what happens when the selection does not land.
//
// Every step announces itself, so whichever overhead is the last one you see is the step that
// hung. Run this with the shelf closed, then again with it already open, and compare.

clearall
clearsysmsg
cleardragdrop
clearignore

@setvar! wait__short 300
@setvar! wait__long 1000
@setvar! wait__target 2000
@setvar! config__reach 2

if not varexist global__my_storage_shelf or not find global__my_storage_shelf ground -1 -1 config__reach
    unsetvar global__my_storage_shelf
    overhead "Target the storage shelf" 55
    setvar global__my_storage_shelf
endif

// Start from a clean slate: a cursor or a gump left by something else would be picked up here.
if targetexists
    overhead "0 cancelling a cursor that was already up" 33
    hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
    wait wait__short
endif

gumpclose
wait wait__short

overhead "1 menu 1" 55
menu global__my_storage_shelf 1

overhead "2 waiting for a cursor" 55
waitfortarget wait__target

if targetexists
    overhead "3 cursor came, answering self" 63
    target self
    wait wait__short
else
    overhead "3 no cursor came" 33
endif

wait wait__long

if targetexists
    overhead "4 a cursor is still up" 33
    hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
    wait wait__short
else
    overhead "4 no cursor left" 63
endif

gumpclose
wait wait__short
overhead "5 finished" 63
